Under identical conditions, $\dfrac{r_1}{r_2} = \sqrt{\dfrac{M_2}{M_1}}$. As rate is inversely proportional to time, $\dfrac{t_2}{t_1} = \sqrt{\dfrac{M_2}{M_1}}$

(a) For He, $t_2 = \sqrt{\frac{4}{2}}(5\ \text{s}) = 5\sqrt{2}$ s $\neq 10$ s;

(b) For $\text{O}_2$, $t_2 = \sqrt{\frac{32}{2}}(5\ \text{s}) = 20$ s

(c) For CO, $t_2 = \sqrt{\frac{28}{2}}(5\ \text{s}) \neq 25$ s;

(d) For $\text{CO}_2$, $t_2 = \sqrt{\frac{44}{2}}(5\ \text{s}) \neq 55$ s
